Subject: Help needed-fast!

My Mom has a relative who recovered completely from "incurable"
cancer ( I think it was the pancreas but I can check) after adopting a
macrobiotic diet.
  I wouldn't eschew traditional medicine in favor of diet, but it 
probably can't hurt. My personal suspicion is that the diet is
healthy, but that a lot of the cure comes from the belief in the cure.
Keeping a strict diet gives a person something they can actively do 
for their health and focusses them on a positive activity.
  (Why is it, I wonder, that medical science is so quick to acknowledge
that depression can make people ill, and even that people can will 
themselved to die, but very rarely investigates any possible link 
between optimism and healing? I don't have any firm opinions on this,
but there seems to be enough anecdotal evidence to justify further
study.)


