This particular post and your others in response to my "Brave New Extropia"
thread makes me think that you are stuck in your own vision of maleness.  
Since no one else has challenged you on it, allow me.

First: The personality traits that you listed above, are in *all* of us,
women as well as men. While it's true that sociological factors had a big
part in how these traits expressed themselves, you are missing a big part
of the picture if you focus on these traits as being "male behaviors." If 
you substitute "left-handed" for male and "right-handed" for female, you
would see how absurd your statements sound.

Second: *Many* personality traits and behaviors are important in studying the
modern technological fields. The ones you listed above are a *small* subset
of the ones that are important.  Here is a list of some other personality 
traits that I think are just as important. In parenthesis, I list a Jungian
archetype that is often associated with these traits.

	1) Trust, Optimism	(Innocent)
	2) Interdependence, Realism   (Orphan)
	3) Autonomy, Ambition   (Seeker)
	4) Passion, Commitment  (Lover)
	5) Individuality   (Creator)
	6) Responsibility  (Ruler)
	7) Wisdom, Non-attachment   (Sage)

I don't think you are going to get very far with territoriality, 
aggressiveness, and testing limits behaviors unless you invoke these other 
aspects of yourself.

